  "abstract": "This submission is a precise replication of Lumina I's new global SOTA model, \"Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Learnable Gamma Ramp (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05)\" (ID 443, score -0.026125). It incorporates the key innovation of a learnable `gamma` ramp within the `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` architecture, allowing the model to adaptively shape the temporal weighting of the Fourier output. All other hyperparameters, including `proj_rank=36`, `mlp_hidden_size=160x2`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, and `optax.adam(eps=1e-8)` with gradient clipping, are precisely matched. This aims to accurately reproduce the global SOTA and establish a new lineage baseline. This run benefits from the new 60-minute trial timeout.",
